## Skills System

Another major newer addition is the expanded skills subsystem.

The loop now supports:

- legacy executable markdown skills in `.agent/skills/*.md`
- standards-based `SKILL.md` directory skills

It can load standard skills from:

- `skills/`
- `.agents/skills/`
- `.agent/skills/`
- `.claude/skills/`

Repo-local `skills/` is the preferred first-class directory.

The system does two kinds of skill work:

1. Executable tool-skills
   - reusable JS or command-backed extensions
   - dynamically callable by the loop

2. Reference skills
   - `SKILL.md` procedural guidance
   - selected by relevance
   - injected into context when useful

This is a strong design choice because it allows the agent to combine:

- runtime tools
- reusable procedures
- repo-owned operational knowledge

without hardwiring everything into the base prompt.

